{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB01204 - MONDO_19457",
  "verbalization": "Mitoxantrone, a蒽醌-based anthracycline antibiotic, is associated with the indication of Unclassified Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) and, through a series of indications, links to Therapy Related AML and Myelodysplastic Syndrome (tAML-MyDPS). The evidence suggests that Mitoxantrone may be repurposed for tAML-MyDPS, as it is implicated in the pathogenesis of AML through its anti-cancer activity. The mechanism of action is likely mediated by mitoxantrone's ability to induce DNA damage and trigger apoptosis in leukemic cells, which is supported by its association with Ivosidenib and Decitabine, both of which are known to modulate gene expression and have anti-leukemic effects. The presence of multiple pathways converging on tAML-MyDPS indicates a potential role for Mitoxantrone in the treatment of this condition, particularly in cases where conventional therapies are ineffective. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of targeting the underlying molecular mechanisms of AML, such as DNA repair and cell cycle regulation, which are frequently dysregulated in these diseases.",
